# Review: MeetingRecorderPlugin

The plugin is fully built: the four operations, the recorder state machine, the settings, the status-bar
item, the native mic detector (Rust `meeting-capture` crate in composer-app) and the two-channel
`MeetingSession` that segments each source with a `SpeakingMonitor` and falls back to the microphone
when system audio is refused. The code matches the spec closely; the gap is tests. Only the pure
pieces are tested: the ignore-list and naming policy (`policy.test.ts`), the elapsed-time format, and
the Rust detector's self-exclusion and diffing. No test drives the operations or the state machine, so
nearly every behavioural verdict is `untested` and the scenarios are at best partly covered.

Minor divergences: `RecorderState` is a tagged union with an extra `stopRequested` flag on
`starting`, and the built-in ignore list lives in `DEFAULT_IGNORED_APPS` with `ignoredApps` only
adding to it rather than defaulting to it.

